{
  "dom_id": "questionExplanation-83246",
  "name": null,
  "problem": "",
  "worked_solution": "To calculate the average value of the velocity on $[{t}_{1},{t}_{2}],$ we use the average value formula\n\n$$\n{v}_{\\text{avg}}=\\frac{1}{{t}_{2}-{t}_{1}}{\\int }_{{t}_{1}}^{{t}_{2}}v(t)\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\nSo, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{v}_{\\text{avg}} & =\\frac{1}{6-2}\\,{\\int }_{2}^{6}(\\frac{{2}^{t}}{12})\\text{d}t \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4\\cdot 12\\cdot \\operatorname{ln}⁡2}({2}^{t}){|}_{2}^{6} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{48\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}({2}^{6}-{2}^{2}) \\\\  & =\\frac{60}{48\\operatorname{ln}⁡2} \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{4\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the average velocity is $\\frac{5}{4\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}\\,\\text{m/s}.$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
  "fields": [],
  "problem_field_keys": [],
  "answer_fields_complete": null,
